/** Tex's graph in words, as every Tex agent reads it (`texArchitecture.js`). */
export const TEX_MAP = "Tex is a graph of steps (nodes) joined by wires, both read from Tex's config (texConfig.json), which is what runs. A step is code or one model call. A wire says what runs next and on what: \"then\" runs the next step on this one's output, only when its condition holds; \"may call\" lets a step call another and wait for the answer; \"may send work back to\" returns a draft for another try; \"may start as a background job\" starts work that reports later; \"afterwards, in the background\" runs once the text has gone, with nobody waiting.\n\nA turn starts at one of: Check-in; Routine runs; Send through Tex; A text arrives; Old number intake; A text is edited or unsent; Staff move a chat; Nightly; Staff messages.\n\n- Check-in (code, no model): Three times a day, look at what changed in their workspace, mail and calendar, and text them only what can't wait; most looks stay quiet. Runs the front door with its own read-only tools and setup model.\n  then: Front door (when look)\n- Routine runs (code, no model): Start a routine (a note under tex/routines/) on its schedule as a routine, not as a text: gather the routine, its past runs and when the person last reacted to or answered one, so Front door knows it's a routine, judges whether it is still relevant or stale, and asks the person whether to keep it when nobody has engaged with it.\n  then: Front door (when run); Confirmations & refusals (when stopped)\n- Send through Tex (code, no model): Another AI connected to Context asks Tex to text the person (send notify) because something needs them now; their settings decide whether it goes, and it is texted as written, with no model.\n  then: Text them (when send)\nIntake (a group of steps): A text arrives, A text is edited or unsent, Triage, Decide, Queue, React, Door.\n- A text arrives (code, no model): Take every text, picture or tapback from iMessage or WhatsApp and get it into the chat's record before anything decides about it.\n  then: Triage\n- Old number intake (code, no model): When staff have switched Tex's old Sendblue line to redirect, a text that arrives on it takes no turn and gets one short reply naming the new number, at most once a day per chat (later texts that day are held); every other text goes on to Triage.\n  then: Text them (when redirect)\n- A text is edited or unsent (code, no model): When someone edits or unsends a text they sent (iMessage Edit and Undo Send, on the Photon line; Sendblue sends neither), keep it in the chat beside the text it changes. An edit that changes nothing does nothing; any other edit goes on to Triage as a text of its own, marked as the edit, and Decide judges it from its examples (a fixed typo can go quiet, a changed ask gets its answer). An unsent text is kept as taken back and leaves the queue if Tex has not started on it, with no turn.\n  then: Triage (when turn)\nStaff messages (a group of steps): Staff move a chat, Staff messages.\n- Staff move a chat (code, no model): Staff move one chat at a time to Tex's new number from the console (Platform → Lines); once a minute the texting Worker takes the moves asked for, and this words the one text the old line sends: a person is told to text the new number from now on, a group that Tex is swapping numbers. A group first gets the new number added (Sendblue), then the note from the old number; when the new line hears that note among the same people (read from the bridge, since its event names only the sender) it ties the two groups together, so the group keeps its home and memory, and takes the old number out. No model; with no new number saved, nothing is sent.\n  then: Text them (when person, group)\n- Triage (code, no model): Code's rules before any judge: one text with nothing of Tex's waiting on it, a command, a setting or a yes code goes straight to the queue; several texts, a bare thanks, or a text that may leave an ask behind goes to Decide. In a group, a command said to Tex goes straight on, and every other line goes to Decide.\n  then: Decide (when judge, running); Queue (when tex)\n  may stop, restart or give its go to: Door as a provisional run (revertible) (when stop:running)\n- Decide (Clef): Choose, from labelled examples, whether this text gets an answer, a reaction, a short wait or nothing, so Tex never answers what wasn't for it.\n  then: React; Queue\n  may stop, restart or give its go to: Door as a provisional run (revertible) (when stop:quiet, restart:wait)\n- Queue (code, no model): Keep one turn per chat at a time (groups up to three side by side) so two answers never race each other.\n  may stop, restart or give its go to: Door as a provisional run (revertible)\nTurned off (deleted after Promote) (a group of steps): Read the text, Run a routine, Check the question, Settle a yes or no, Watch what leaves, Check it may run, Read the history, Open the web, Read the setup, Bookkeeping, Prepare the answer, Router, Fallback, Big-ask planner, Answer checks, Reply reviewer, Classifier, Self-review, Job check, Advisor on job mail, Memory nudge, Reflect.\n- Read the text (code, no model, turned off: never runs): Read the request: who is asking, from which chat, and what they asked.\n- Run a routine (code, no model, turned off: never runs): For a routine's run: reload the routine, and stop here when it is paused or its job needs no model.\n- Check the question (code, no model, turned off: never runs): Check the question and what came with it: the files, the message it replies to, the tapbacks.\n- Settle a yes or no (code, no model, turned off: never runs): A texted yes or no settles a waiting approval here, in code, before any model runs.\n- Watch what leaves (code, no model, turned off: never runs): Start this turn's egress ledger: what it reads from outside and what it may send out.\n- Check it may run (code, no model, turned off: never runs): Start reading the tools and the history, and check the model may run here.\n- Read the history (code, no model, turned off: never runs): Hear voice messages, keep sent files, and read the chat's history and the tools offered.\n- Open the web (code, no model, turned off: never runs): Pick the write tools for this chat and open the browser, vouched for by the person's own words.\n- Read the setup (code, no model, turned off: never runs): Read Tex's setup: its prompt, history length, skills, models, router and fallback.\n- Bookkeeping (code, no model, turned off: never runs): Prepare what the turn records: usage, the turn log, the ledger turn id, the pictures to keep.\n- Prepare the answer (code, no model, turned off: never runs): Start the side read of Tex's notes and set up the answer checks and pictures.\n- Router (Clef, turned off: never runs): Send a plain lookup to a cheaper path and keep the front door for changes and thinking.\n- Front door (Haiku 5.5): Write Tex's answer: read the chat, call the tools that do the work, and draft the reply.\n  then: Answer check\n  may call: Tools (when action); Big-ask planner (when big)\n  may start as a background job: Background job (when job)\n- Fallback (GLM-4.7 Flash, turned off: never runs): Answer when the front door's model is down, so a text never goes unanswered.\n- Big-ask planner (Opus 5.5, turned off: never runs): Break a big ask into steps before the front door starts, so it doesn't wander.\nTools & subagents (a group of steps): Tools, Advisor, Mail checker, Card check, Egress judge, Picture maker.\n- Tools (code, no model): Do the actual work in Context and the world: read, write, manage and send. Added only in code.\n  may call: Mail checker (when email); Card check (when card); Egress judge (when share); Picture maker (when picture); Advisor (when ask_advisor)\n- Advisor (Opus 5.5): Think harder when the front door is stuck, and say what to try next.\n- Answer checks (code, no model, turned off: never runs): Catch what code can prove wrong in a draft (a claim with no call behind it, a figure in nothing the model saw, a missing link) before a model looks.\n- Mail checker (Haiku 5.5): Read an email before it goes and stop one that is wrong, rude or to the wrong person.\n- Card check (Haiku 5.5): Check a card's fields match what was asked before it is shown.\n- Reply reviewer (Haiku 5.5, turned off: never runs): Read the draft as the person would and send it back when it misses, so they never get a wrong or lazy answer.\n- Text them (code, no model): Deliver the answer: the texts, any card, and a reaction, as the chat's service allows.\n  afterwards, in the background, nobody waiting: Learn (when fired); After the reply (when sent, threads); Chat day summaries (when sent, ended, answered)\n- React (code, no model): Put Decide's tapback on their text straight away, so a thanks or a win gets a reaction without a reply.\n- Classifier (Haiku 5.5, turned off: never runs): File each text into a conversation thread after the reply, so later turns see a short index instead of everything.\n- Self-review (Haiku 5.5, turned off: never runs): Look back at a sent answer and note what to do better next time.\nJobs (a group of steps): Background job, Hand-back judge, Job advisor.\n- Background job (Haiku 5.5): Do long work (browsing, forms, many steps) without holding up the reply.\n  may call: Job advisor (when job); Tools (when job)\n  may start as a background job: Hand-back judge (when job)\n- Job check (Opus 5.5, turned off: never runs): Check a job's work as it goes and steer it when it drifts.\n- Advisor on job mail (Opus 5.5, turned off: never runs): Decide what to tell the person when a job gets mail it can't handle alone.\n- Hand-back judge (Haiku 5.5): Make sure what a job hands back is true and finished before the person hears it.\n- Egress judge (Haiku 5.5): Let a step that widens who can see something, or acts in the person's name, run only when the person's own words ask for it; anything but a clear yes is a no.\n- Picture maker (google/gemini-2.5-flash-image): Draw a card or graphic, or make a photo with Gemini, for a texted answer; every one is looked at by Card check before it may go.\n  may call: Card check\n- Memory nudge (Haiku 5.5, turned off: never runs): Every ten texts, or when an answer was about them, write what was learned into About me now instead of waiting for the dream.\n- Reflect (Haiku 5.5, turned off: never runs): After a hard or corrected turn, write down what worked as a learned skill for next time.\n- Nightly (code, no model): Start each night's work for a person: the dream and the summaries of their days, and housekeeping, each on the schedule the control plane keeps.\n  then: Dream (when dream); Housekeeping (when housekeeping)\n- Dream (Haiku 5.5): Read the chat since the last dream and the memories that fit, and keep About me true: add what was learned, take out what is no longer so.\n  then: Day summaries (when summarize)\n- Day summaries (Haiku 5.5): Sum up each finished day of the chat not yet summed up, into the chat's ledger, for later turns.\n- Housekeeping (Haiku 5.5): Tidy their workspace once a day within its time limit: fix what the health check names, change nothing it cannot undo, and log each change.\n- Door (code, no model): Gather what the turn needs (the text, routine, question, yes or no, what may leave, may it run, history, web, setup, bookkeeping) in code before any model runs; each part logged inside this step.\n  then: Front door (when next); Confirmations & refusals (when answered)\n- Staff messages (code, no model): Texts staff send through Tex from the console, such as the note that a chat is moving to Tex's new number; no model, worded in code, out through Bypass.\n  then: Staff move a chat (when move)\n- Job advisor (Opus 5.5): Check a job's work as it goes and steer it when it drifts; advise on mail the job drafts before it leaves.\n- Learn (Haiku 5.5): After a texted turn, write what was learned: About me every ten texts or when the answer was about them, and a learned skill after a hard or corrected turn.\n- After the reply (Haiku 5.5): After the reply, file each text into a conversation thread and score the conversation, filing a review when something went wrong.\n- Answer check (Haiku 5.5): Check a draft before it goes: code first catches what it can prove wrong (a claim with no call behind it, a figure nothing showed, a missing link); for a report or routine a model then reads it as the person would. Either can send it back to the front door.\n  then: Text them\n  may send work back to: Front door\n- Confirmations & refusals (code, no model): Answers the door settles in code, with no model: a yes, no or thumbs-up to something Tex is waiting on (including a computer step), and the short refusals (a request that can't be read, a question too long, not allowed to run, the model unavailable). Logs which one and why, then hands it to Text them.\n  then: Text them\n- Chat day summaries (Haiku 5.5): After a reply, sum up each finished day of this chat (1:1 or group) in the last 3 weeks not yet summed up, 3 a run, into the chat's ledger, for the 7-day history to show before the last 7 days.";
